  "name": "Turn Google Trends into LinkedIn, Facebook and Bluesky posts with Perplexity and PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c4a82ddd-a7bc-4aac-ab50-06f722336e07",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -643,
        -121
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 803,
        "content": "## Turn today's Google Trends into researched posts\nEvery weekday Perplexity picks the one trending search your brand can join, researches why it is trending, and PostWire writes and publishes a native post for LinkedIn, Facebook and Bluesky.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every weekday at 8:00** reads the Google Trends RSS feed for your country (free, no key). **Skip trends already used** drops any trend seen on a previous day.\n2. **Research with Perplexity** searches the web, picks the trend that fits your niche and returns why it is trending, two facts and an angle, with the pages it read. It skips tragedies, politics and private people.\n3. **On brand?** stops the run when no trend fits, so nothing is posted.\n4. **Post to LinkedIn, Facebook, Bluesky** (PostWire) writes a different post for each network from the research and publishes them.\n5. **Log the post** adds a row per network with its link and the sources. A refusal goes to **Log the failure**, and **Email me the fix** sends what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Fill in **Set your brand and niche**: brand, niche, country code (US, GB, DE...) and your email.\n3. Add a Perplexity API credential (a research request costs a few cents).\n4. Create a sheet with the columns date, trend, network, status, link, sources and note, and pick it in both Sheets nodes. Connect Gmail.\n\n### Customize\nChange the hour in the trigger, the safety rules in the Perplexity instructions, or the networks in the PostWire node (the free PostWire plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
